From c52bb8d54309f4d0b7a5ef5393602c1bf753082f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Mar 2026 09:17:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 142/913] stm32mp15 tree wide: use DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM() for
 MP15

Replace DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER() directives with DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()
for resources that need to be unpaged for PM sequence support. This
change covers the resources used by generic core and stm32mp15
platforms.

Also add few keep.h inclusions that are missing.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 09284d2cf11f4ff12ce3b6209864634ee1a4bedf stm32mp15 tree wide: use DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM() for MP15]
Change-Id: I4e847ab0a19e5b290b083ef8e0a5aa436b32840f
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/392007
Domain-Review: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>

